{
 "manufacturer": "Woodward",
 "manufacturer_slug": "woodward",
 "model": "easYgen-1000 Series genset controller (Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "easygen-1000",
 "short_model": "easYgen-1000",
 "aliases": [
  "easYgen-1000",
  "easYgen1000",
  "easYgen-1000 Series"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Generator controller",
 "applies_to": "easYgen-1000 series software version 2.1xxx, transmission telegram protocol 4003, per interface manual 37393B.",
 "summary": "The easYgen-1000 is Woodward's genset controller for single units and AMF duty. On RS-485 it is a Modbus RTU slave: the visualization telegram (protocol 4003) is block-read from Modicon 450001, and control word 1 at parameter 503 starts, stops and acknowledges the set. This map covers generator and mains voltages, currents and frequency, energy and hours counters, status and alarm words, a few J1939 engine values and the remote-control word.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "The manual uses Modicon numbers. Telegram word No. n is Modicon 450000 + n; the manual says 450001 may become bus address 50000, so word n is wire address 49999 + n. Parameters use Modicon 40000 + (parameter ID + 1), so control word 1 (parameter 503) is 40504 = wire address 503."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": "2.1xxx",
 "source": {
  "title": "easYgen-1000 Series Interfaces - Interface Description, Software Version 2.1xxx",
  "doc_number": "37393B",
  "revision_date": "2008-07-02",
  "url": "https://www.woodward.com/products/publication-asset/37393",
  "pages": "pp. 10-11 (telegrams), pp. 13-19 (Modbus RTU slave, addressing, parameters, exceptions), pp. 41-52 (transmission telegram), p. 53 (remote control telegram)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "32-bit values are listed as a High word row followed by a Low word row, so the high word sits at the lower address (ABCD).",
  "The telegram prints units and resolution but no signed/unsigned type. Voltages, currents, frequency, energy and hours cannot be negative, so the unsigned type here reads them correctly either way.",
  "Left out: generator and mains real power, reactive power and power factor (words 10, 13, 50, 53, 56, 59, 61-65), because the telegram does not say whether they are signed and they can go negative; analog inputs T1/T2 (no scaling given); hours/days until maintenance; the system state bits 0-5 of word 34, whose labels sit between two bit rows; diagnostic (DM1/DM2) SPN/FMT words and most J1939 engine values.",
  "Words 112-168 come from an engine ECU over J1939 and only hold data when one is connected and configured.",
  "Parameters (configuration range 40001-450000) are read or written one at a time with a length that matches the parameter data type; the full parameter list is in configuration manual 37391, not this document."
 ],
